"- Inner Bottle Wall\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A smooth, curved internal surface forming the inner boundary of the bottle neck.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Dark, almost black with subtle amber or coppery reflections along the rim due to light refraction.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The inner wall extends from the central aperture outward to the glass rim; its radial width is not explicitly measurable but appears consistent with standard bottle neck dimensions.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Glass, exhibiting a glossy, reflective finish.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of transparent glass with slight surface texture or residue visible near the rim.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One continuous inner wall surface.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Occupies the inner circumference of the bottle neck, directly surrounding the central aperture.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - Curved inward, concentrically aligned with the central aperture.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - Attached to and seamlessly transitions into the glass rim and central aperture.\n\n- Glass Rim\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A circular, raised edge at the opening of the bottle neck, forming the outermost boundary of the aperture.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Dark brown to black with golden-orange highlights along the top edge due to light reflection.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The rim is approximately 1-2 mm thick, with a circular diameter matching the bottle’s opening.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Glass, with a polished and slightly reflective surface.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Made of glass with visible surface imperfections or residue near the inner edge.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One continuous rim.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Positioned at the outermost edge of the bottle neck, encircling the central aperture.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - Horizontally oriented, forming a circular boundary.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - Connected to the inner bottle wall and the central aperture, forming the structural edge of the bottle opening.\n\n- Bottle Neck Opening\n    - Attribute 1 Type - The circular opening at the top of the bottle neck, defined by the glass rim and inner wall.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Dark, appearing black or very dark brown, with subtle reflective highlights along the rim.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The opening is circular, with a diameter that appears consistent with standard bottle neck dimensions.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Glass, transparent but tinted dark.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of glass with visible surface texture or residue near the rim.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One opening.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Located at the center of the image, surrounded by the glass rim and inner bottle wall.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - Circular and centered, facing directly toward the viewer.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - Connected to the glass rim and inner bottle wall, forming the functional aperture of the bottle.\n\n- Central Aperture\n    - Attribute 1 Type - The hollow, dark central void within the bottle neck opening.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Deep black, with no visible internal features or reflections.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - Circular, with a diameter slightly smaller than the bottle neck opening, defined by the inner bottle wall.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Glass, but the aperture itself is an empty space within the glass structure.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of the absence of material, surrounded by glass.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One central aperture.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Located at the center of the bottle neck, surrounded by the inner bottle wall and glass rim.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - Circular and centered, aligned with the bottle’s axis.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - Connected to the inner bottle wall and glass rim, forming the central void of the bottle neck."